  "content": {
    "id": "p45-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Find how many arrangements of the letters of the word TRANSITION are possible if:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q14-paired-parts",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "there are no restrictions",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$453\\,600$",
              "worked": "There are 10 letters, with I, T and N each appearing twice.\n$$\\frac{10!}{2!\\,2!\\,2!}=453\\,600$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "the Is are together",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$90\\,720$",
              "worked": "Treat II as one unit. There are 9 objects, with T twice and N twice.\n$$\\frac{9!}{2!\\,2!}=90\\,720$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "the Is are together, and so are the Ns, and so are the Ts",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$5040$",
              "worked": "Treat II, NN and TT as units. The resulting 7 objects are distinct.\n$$7!=5040$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 15
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "the Ns occupy the end positions",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$10\\,080$",
              "worked": "Fix an N at each end. The 8 middle positions contain I twice and T twice.\n$$\\frac{8!}{2!\\,2!}=10\\,080$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "an N occupies the first but not the last position",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$80\\,640$",
              "worked": "Fix the first position as N. The other N has 8 possible positions, excluding the last position. Fill the remaining 8 positions, with I twice and T twice.\n$$8\\times\\frac{8!}{2!\\,2!}=80\\,640$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 26
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q14-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "the letter N is not at either end",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$282\\,240$",
              "worked": "Subtract the three disjoint cases from the unrestricted total: N at the first end only, N at the last end only, and N at both ends.\nFrom part e, each one-end-only case has $80\\,640$ arrangements. From part d, the both-ends case has $10\\,080$ arrangements.\n$$\\begin{aligned}453\\,600-80\\,640-80\\,640-10\\,080&=282\\,240\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 33
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q14-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "the vowels are together",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15\\,120$",
          "worked": "Treat the vowels I, I, A and O as one unit. There are 7 objects, with T twice and N twice.\nArrange the units:\n$$\\frac{7!}{2!\\,2!}$$\nArrange the vowels within their unit:\n$$\\frac{4!}{2!}$$\nTotal:\n$$\\frac{7!}{2!\\,2!}\\times\\frac{4!}{2!}=15\\,120$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
